docs {
  # 03. List Expenses

  **Method:** `GET`
  **Endpoint:** `/api/v1/groups/:groupID/expenses`
  **Auth:** Required

  ## Description

  Returns active (not soft-deleted) expenses with full splits, caller permissions and caller share. The item structure matches Get Expense. Ordered by occurred_at DESC NULLS LAST, then id DESC. Pagination.total counts expenses. Existing attachment-demo expense records are preserved by migration; they can have shares=[] until explicitly updated with a valid split. No allocation is invented for legacy records.

  All routes require a valid access token, ACTIVE account and ACTIVE membership with left_at=null. A user who left or was removed cannot read, create, edit or delete expenses, even their own. ACTIVE and INACTIVE are the membership status values currently returned by this project; left and removed members remain stored as INACTIVE, normally with left_at set.

  SETTLING and CLOSED groups allow expense reads only. is_frozen=true and can_edit/can_delete=false in that state. On an active group, only the expense creator or current group owner can edit/delete. Site ADMIN alone does not override membership or editing permissions.

  Amounts are integer TOMAN. expense_type is a separate legacy enum (NORMAL, PREMIUM); new records are NORMAL. split_type is the allocation enum (EQUAL, EXACT, PERCENTAGE, WEIGHTED). No wallet charge or premium purchase is performed here.

  ## Request

  Path groupID is a positive BIGINT group ID. expenseID, when present, is a positive expense ID in that same group. Use the manual expenseGroupId and expenseId environment variables.

  Query parameters are optional. `page` defaults to 1. `limit` defaults to 20 and accepts 1–100.

  | Expense tab | scope | What it returns |
  | --- | --- | --- |
  | Group expenses | `all` (default) | All non-deleted expenses in the group. |
  | Expenses I recorded | `created_by_me` | Expenses created by the caller's membership in this group. |
  | Expenses I owe a share of | `owed_by_me` | Expenses paid by another member where the caller has a positive, non-deleted share. |

  Scope values are lowercase and case-sensitive. For example, send `?scope=owed_by_me&page=1&limit=20`. The backend filters before paginating, and `pagination.total` counts matching expenses. `owed_by_me` reports the original expense shares. Settlements do not change this list or its share amounts.

  ## Response

  **200 OK**

  ```json
  {
    "success": true,
    "data": {
      "items": [
        {
          "id": 1101,
          "group_id": 10,
          "created_by_member_id": 30,
          "paid_by_member_id": 30,
          "title": "Dinner",
          "description": "Dinner after the trip",
          "total_amount_toman": 100,
          "expense_type": "NORMAL",
          "split_type": "EQUAL",
          "occurred_at": "2026-11-16T10:00:00Z",
          "created_at": "2026-11-16T10:01:00Z",
          "updated_at": "2026-11-16T10:01:00Z",
          "is_frozen": false,
          "can_edit": true,
          "can_delete": true,
          "shares": [
            {
              "member_id": 30,
              "value": 1,
              "share_amount_toman": 34
            },
            {
              "member_id": 31,
              "value": 1,
              "share_amount_toman": 33
            },
            {
              "member_id": 32,
              "value": 1,
              "share_amount_toman": 33
            }
          ],
          "my_share_amount_toman": 34,
          "attachment_ids": [],
          "attachments": []
        }
      ],
      "pagination": {
        "page": 1,
        "limit": 20,
        "total": 1
      }
    }
  }
  ```

  attachments contains receipt metadata (id, original_filename, mime_type, file_size_bytes) and access_url. attachment_ids remains the matching ID list. Both arrays are [] when empty. URLs are signed and expire (15 minutes by default); refetch this endpoint or Get Attachment Details for a fresh URL. The server never makes receipts public.

  ## Errors

  | HTTP | code | error | When |
  | --- | --- | --- | --- |
  | 400 | `BAD_REQUEST` | `bad request payload or parameters` | Invalid group ID, pagination, or scope. |
  | 401 | `MISSING_TOKEN` | `authorization token is missing` | Authorization is absent or does not contain a Bearer token. |
  | 401 | `TOKEN_INVALID` | `authorization token is invalid` | Access token is invalid or malformed. |
  | 401 | `TOKEN_EXPIRED` | `authorization token has expired` | Access token expired. |
  | 401 | `TOKEN_REVOKED` | `authorization token has been revoked` | Access token is blacklisted. |
  | 403 | `USER_INACTIVE` | `user account is deactivated` | Authenticated account is not ACTIVE. |
  | 403 | `EXPENSE_FORBIDDEN` | `only active group members can access expenses` | Requester is not an ACTIVE member, or left_at is not null. This also applies to a former expense creator. |
  | 404 | `USER_NOT_FOUND` | `user not found` | Authenticated account no longer exists. |
  | 404 | `GROUP_NOT_FOUND` | `group not found` | Group does not exist or is soft-deleted. |
  | 500 | `INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR` | `an internal server error occurred` | Database or authentication infrastructure failed; causes remain private. |
  | 503 | `STORAGE_UNAVAILABLE` | `storage service is temporarily unavailable` | Receipt or avatar URL generation failed. |
}
